                     /note="MftR, the mycofactocin system transcriptional
                     regulator, is an uncharacterized TetR family DNA-binding
                     transcription factor. Its role is inferred by context. It
                     occurs as part of the biosynthesis locus for mycofactocin,
                     a partially characterized electron carrier derived from
                     the terminal Val-Tyr dipeptide of the precursor peptide
                     MftA, through a radical SAM enzyme-mediated process;
                     Derived by automated computational analysis using gene
                     prediction method: Protein Homology."
