                     /GO_process="GO:0140604 - mycofactocin biosynthetic
                     process [Evidence IEA]"
                     /note="MftB, a small protein, is a peptide chaperone that
                     assists the radical SAM enzyme MftC in performing two
                     modifications to the C-terminal Val-Tyr dipeptide of the
                     mycofactocin precursor peptide, MftA. MftB's role is
                     analogous to the role of PqqD in the biosynthesis of PQQ,
                     a cofactor that derives entirely from a Tyr and a Glu in
                     the precursor PqqA; Derived by automated computational
                     analysis using gene prediction method: Protein Homology."
